<title>INDIA: Indian soybean prices steady on low volumes.</title>
<headline>Indian soybean prices steady on low volumes.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1996-09-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indian soybean prices were steady on Friday on low volumes, dealers said.</p>
<p>The new season's soybean from Sangli, delivered at Indore was quoted at 12,950-13,000 per tonne with arrivals being around 1,500 tonnes a day.</p>
<p>Soyoil refined was steady while soyoil solvent gained by 100 rupees on increased industrial demand.</p>
<p>Soymeal yellow was firm on good export demand. Soymeal yellow was $303-304 ready delivery for current season and was $283-284 per tonne in export. Rapeseed extraction was $130-132 per tonne in export. Rapeseed extraction was 4,500 rupees FOR Bedibunder and was 4,450 rupees per tonne FOR Bhavnagar.</p>
<p>The markets are closed on Monday for a Hindu festival.</p>
